within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.A_AlimentaryTractAndMetabolism.A10B_BloodGlucoseLoweringDrugsExclInsulins.A10BA02_Metformin;
model Metformin_Stepensky2002_PD_r
  "indirect_response_i exposure-response sweep — Stepensky_2002 :: R (blood glucose levels)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Interfaces.PartialExposureResponseSweep(
    E0 = 383.763837638,      // [mg/100 ml]
    Emax = 0.486,  // type I effect term
    EC50 = 4.31e-07,  // [kg; µg × 1e-09]
    gamma = 2,
    exposure_per_s = 1e-09);   // 1 µg per second
equation
  response = E0*(1 - Emax*frac);   // steady state, indirect response type I
  // e0_from_kin_kout: no baseline row; E0 = kin/kout (2.08/0.00542 = 383.8) — the paper's stated baseline may differ
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 4400, Interval = 8.8),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Metformin_Stepensky2002_PD_r</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Stepensky D et al., <i>Drug metabolism and disposition: the biological fate of chemicals 30(8):861–868</i> 2002 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1124/dmd.30.8.861\">doi:10.1124/dmd.30.8.861</a>) — blood glucose levels [mg/100 ml] against metformin µg — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: indirect_response_i.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    = 383.763837638 mg/100 ml drug-free response (baseline) (kin/kout, Q327/Q328)
  Emax  =      0.486          maximal effect term (E_max GI, Q323)
  EC50  =        431 µg       exposure at half of the maximal effect term (EA_50 GI, Q321)
  gamma =          2          Hill coefficient (n_GI, Q325)</pre><p>The algebra is <code>response = E0*(1 - Emax*frac)</code>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one µg of metformin per second of simulated time (exposure is in kg): there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 383.8   (drug-free)
  exposure = EC50 (431 µg)  response 290.5
  exposure -> infinity  response 197.3</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Stepensky_2002: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Metformin_Stepensky2002_PD_r;
